course: dictionary
lesson: 13858
title: Wise choices: the word judicious
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Judicious is a formal word. It means wise and sensible, showing good judgement. Someone who is judicious has thought carefully before they act or choose.
explain: «She made a judicious choice and packed a raincoat, because the sky looked grey.» Packing a coat for a grey sky is sensible, so judicious means wise and careful, not rushed.
explain: «The gardener made judicious use of the water, so the plants survived the dry summer.» Judicious use means using something carefully, without wasting it. Try swapping in wise or sensible: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: The adverb is judiciously, as in «Ella spent her pocket money judiciously, saving some for later.» It tells you how she spent it: wisely and carefully.
fact: Judicious means wise and sensible, showing good judgement.
fact: Judicious is an adjective, and judiciously is the adverb.
fact: «A judicious choice» is a sensible choice made after careful thought.
fact: «Judicious use of water» means using water carefully, without waste.
fact: Judgement is the ability to decide well. A judicious person has good judgement.
exercise: «The captain made a judicious decision to turn the boat back before the storm.» What does judicious mean here? | Rushed and loud | Funny | *Wise and sensible | Sad and slow
exercise: «Ella spent her pocket money judiciously.» What does judiciously mean? | Loudly and proudly | *Wisely and carefully | Quickly and angrily | Without thinking at all
exercise: «Mum made a judicious choice: she packed a raincoat for the trip.» Find and copy the word that tells you the choice was wise. | trip | raincoat | packed | *judicious
test: What does a judicious plan show? | *Good judgement | Bad luck | Loud voices | A hurry
test: «The team used their time judiciously, so they finished the project before Friday.» What does judiciously mean? | Carelessly and in a rush | *Wisely and carefully | Angrily | Sleepily
exam: Which best describes a judicious person? | Someone who acts without thinking | Someone who never listens to advice | *Someone who weighs up the facts before acting | Someone who shouts at everyone
